From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:24:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: phy: allwinner,sun60i-a733-usb3-combophy: Add
 DisplayPort

The first combo PHY of the A733 SERDES block carries either USB3 or the
four main link lanes of the DisplayPort transmitter to the Type-C
connector (user manual section 18.2.1). Describe the second function.

The PHY becomes a provider with one cell, the PHY type from
dt-bindings/phy/phy.h, as on the Rockchip USBDP and Qualcomm QMP combo
PHYs: PHY_TYPE_USB3 for the USB3 controller, PHY_TYPE_DP for the
DisplayPort transmitter. It can be the mode switch of the connector,
and the board describes the polarity of its lanes per function with
the generic tx-polarity properties.

With all four lanes on DisplayPort the USB3 controller has no SuperSpeed
lanes and still needs a PIPE clock to leave its core soft reset. Add an
optional third clock, the PIPE clock select of the SERDES CCU (user
manual 18.2.6.2), which the PHY enables while it holds the lanes for
DisplayPort.

This changes the device tree ABI: #phy-cells goes from 0 to 1. A kernel
that predates the cell still gets the USB3 function, as its driver
ignores the cell, but no DisplayPort. Without the clock the PHY works as
before, but a USB3 controller that probes while the lanes belong to
DisplayPort fails to start.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board with a device tree that
uses this binding, including the PIPE clock; the combo PHY probes and
enters DisplayPort mode, and dtbs_check reports nothing.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../allwinner,sun60i-a733-usb3-combophy.yaml  | 58 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 46 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/allwinner,sun60i-a733-usb3-combophy.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/allwinner,sun60i-a733-usb3-combophy.yaml
index e49e478a133c..2deb0454b0b4 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/allwinner,sun60i-a733-usb3-combophy.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/allwinner,sun60i-a733-usb3-combophy.yaml
@@ -4,16 +4,22 @@
 $id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/phy/allwinner,sun60i-a733-usb3-combophy.yaml#
 $schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
 
-title: Allwinner A733 USB3 combo PHY
+title: Allwinner A733 USB3 and DisplayPort combo PHY
 
 maintainers:
   - Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
 
 description:
-  The first combo PHY in the SERDES block of the A733 carries the SuperSpeed
-  lanes of the USB3 DRD controller to a USB Type-C connector. The lane swap
-  for a flipped plug is done inside the PHY, so it can act as the orientation
-  switch of the connector.
+  The first combo PHY in the SERDES block of the A733 carries either the
+  SuperSpeed lanes of the USB3 DRD controller or the four main link lanes of
+  the DisplayPort transmitter to a USB Type-C connector. The lane swap for a
+  flipped plug is done inside the PHY, so it can act as the orientation
+  switch of the connector, and the hand-over of the lanes to DisplayPort is
+  done inside the PHY as well, so it can act as the mode switch for
+  DisplayPort alternate mode. While the four lanes are DisplayPort's, the
+  USB3 controller has no SuperSpeed lanes, and the PHY takes the PIPE clock
+  of the controller from the CCU, which the controller needs to leave its
+  core soft reset.
 
 properties:
   compatible:
@@ -33,24 +39,45 @@ properties:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
     description:
       Phandle to the SERDES top registers, a system controller shared with
-      the second combo PHY. It holds the USB3 PIPE clock and RX data muxes
-      and the DisplayPort lane width conversion of this PHY.
+      the second combo PHY. It holds the USB3 PIPE clock and RX data muxes,
+      the DisplayPort lane width conversion and the transmit data lane map
+      of this PHY.
 
   clocks:
+    minItems: 2
     items:
       - description: SERDES PHY clock
       - description: oscillator clock gate of the SERDES
+      - description:
+          PIPE clock select of the SERDES CCU, which takes the PIPE clock of
+          the USB3 controller from the CCU while the lanes carry DisplayPort
 
   clock-names:
+    minItems: 2
     items:
       - const: serdes
       - const: hosc
+      - const: usb3-pipe
 
   resets:
     maxItems: 1
 
   "#phy-cells":
-    const: 0
+    const: 1
+    description:
+      The PHY type, PHY_TYPE_USB3 or PHY_TYPE_DP from
+      dt-bindings/phy/phy.h, selects the function.
+
+  tx-polarity:
+    description:
+      Transmitter polarity of the lanes for each function, as wired on the
+      board.
+    maxItems: 2
+
+  tx-polarity-names:
+    items:
+      - const: dp
+      - const: usb-ss
 
 required:
   - compatible
@@ -63,6 +90,7 @@ required:
   - "#phy-cells"
 
 allOf:
+  - $ref: /schemas/phy/phy-common-props.yaml#
   - $ref: /schemas/usb/usb-switch.yaml#
   - $ref: /schemas/usb/usb-switch-ports.yaml#
 
@@ -71,20 +99,26 @@ unevaluatedProperties: false
 examples:
   - |
     #include <dt-bindings/clock/allwinner,sun60i-a733-ccu.h>
+    #include <dt-bindings/clock/allwinner,sun60i-a733-serdes-ccu.h>
     #include <dt-bindings/clock/sun6i-rtc.h>
+    #include <dt-bindings/phy/phy.h>
     #include <dt-bindings/reset/allwinner,sun60i-a733-ccu.h>
 
     phy@6c01000 {
         compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-usb3-combophy";
-        reg = <0x06c01000 0x1000>,
+        reg = <0x06c01000 0xe00>,
               <0x06c80000 0x20000>;
         reg-names = "link", "pma";
         allwinner,serdes-top = <&serdes_top>;
-        clocks = <&ccu CLK_SERDES_PHY>, <&rtc CLK_HOSC_SERDES0>;
-        clock-names = "serdes", "hosc";
+        clocks = <&ccu CLK_SERDES_PHY>, <&rtc CLK_HOSC_SERDES0>,
+                 <&serdes_ccu CLK_USB3_PIPE_CCU>;
+        clock-names = "serdes", "hosc", "usb3-pipe";
         resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_SERDES>;
-        #phy-cells = <0>;
+        #phy-cells = <1>;
         orientation-switch;
+        mode-switch;
+        tx-polarity = <PHY_POL_INVERT>, <PHY_POL_NORMAL>;
+        tx-polarity-names = "dp", "usb-ss";
 
         port {
             endpoint {
